      "side": 1,
      "message": "Required: the fix premise needs confirmation. Upstream Foreman\u0027s `Hostext::Token` (`refresh_token_on_build`, https://raw.githubusercontent.com/theforeman/foreman/develop/app/models/concerns/hostext/token.rb) calls `set_token` only when `build? !\u003d old.build?`. A `build\u003d1` PUT when Foreman already reports `build\u003dtrue` is token-neutral; this guard skips exactly that PUT, while the false-to-true PUT that rotates the token is still sent. Please confirm the deployed Foreman version and a log where a true-to-true re-mark changes the token. If upstream applies, this is a harmless no-op and the actual fix is the issue\u0027s other items (prepare before power-on, keep token generation close to the reboot, refresh TFTP after a token change); keep #758 open. If your Foreman differs, cite it and the finding can be re-scored.",
      "revId": "3307fb1c62c35f1325f37d320ddfa9062ab9bf4f",
