      "message": "Follow-up: QUADS only ever writes Foreman `build\u003d1`, never `build\u003d0` (standard.py:419 clears only QUADS\u0027 flag), so a failed attempt\u0027s `build\u003dtrue` persists and every retry now skips. That matches the issue\u0027s no-op request, but a host with `token_expired` or a stale token cannot refresh automatically; the documented recovery is manual `build\u003dfalse` then `true`. Consider consulting `build_status`/token expiry and cycling only when the retained token is unusable.",
      "revId": "3307fb1c62c35f1325f37d320ddfa9062ab9bf4f",
