      "side": 1,
      "message": "Follow-up: read-then-PUT is a TOCTOU. Two overlapping rebuilds can both GET `build\u003dfalse` and both PUT; the issue says \u0027retried or overlapping\u0027. There is no per-host serialization. A per-process lock would help within one worker; cross-process coordination needs a different approach. At minimum document the single-runner assumption. Also, Dell/HPE still powers on before `prepare_host_provisioning` (standard.py:192 vs :207); the guard covers the retry when Foreman reports `build\u003dtrue`, but the issue\u0027s ordering window remains a separate item. Consider preparing before power-on or documenting the residual race.",
